#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# manhattan_distance

#% text
# `manhattan_distance(u, v)` gives the sum of the absolute differences of the entries of `u` and `v`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For two numbers it is `abs(u - v)`.

#% item
# Symbolic entries give a sum of absolute values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
manhattan_distance([1, 2], [4, 6])
#% output
#= 7

#% cell
manhattan_distance([a, b], [c, d])
#% output
#= abs(a - c) + abs(b - d)

#% cell
manhattan_distance(3, -2)
#% output
#= 5

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `euclidean_distance`, `distance_matrix`, `norm`
